ed 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp.\n- Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\". That supports funding its +12% capex plan, which is mostly substations and transformers, through debt.\n\n**Equity: weak.**\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity raise because investor demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in Q3.\n\n**Pellham is the weak point.**\n- It is the largest grid-equipment buyer in Caldria, and its 2027 capex plan is up 18%.\n- It has cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferred two substation programmes \"until financing improves\". So the equity shortfall is already reducing spending.\n- Nothing shows that debt alone can fill that gap.\n\n**Gaps.**\n- I found no credit metrics (FFO/debt, ratings headroom) and no data on the 2027 debt maturities, so I can't say whether refinancing crowds out new borrowing.\n- I found no equity valuations or dilution figures.\n- The spread level and the Norvane bond are single data points, not a time series.\n\n**Implication.** Treat 2027 capex, especially Pellham's equipment orders, as at risk of being scaled back. That is negative for grid-equipment suppliers.\n\nThe detailed debt and equity findings are in n5.r1 and n6.r1.","ttft_ms":2478,"type":"result","duration_ms":37996,"uuid":"630bd84c-d961-4f9c-8a07-6bd5fb67f183","ttft_stream_ms":2274,"time_to_request_ms":192,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":41,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":15,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":5,"request_announcements":35,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":11,"tool_schema_build":7,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":8,"request_build":22},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":76,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":76,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"proce